  "notes": "Immortal Empires parchment campaign map - the FRAME MASTER for the IE family, and (world-map-parchment-areas-onto-globe.md, 2026-07-28) the PRIMARY BOUNDARY SOURCE: its interior line network is traced with lettering bridged rather than erased, and its printed names are what the S3a-2 review panel needed. Its three siblings (pizqenw9rd791.jpg, the climate map, the feature image) carry frame_alias records pointing here rather than duplicating these control points, so a correction made here reaches all four. Contributes INTERIOR BOUNDARY LINES AND NAMES ONLY, never coastline (user decision #1/#2, 2026-07-25): tools/derived/land_sea_mask.png is the sole coastline authority, which is what makes a rubber-sheeted registration acceptable - local scale error moves an interior border a few pixels inside a landmass and cannot put a coast in the sea. Hence coastline/relief precedence 5, boundaries 100 - above total_war_map_colored.png's 95, so the parchment's own drawn-and-named cells are the states rather than the flat-filled Total War map. The feature image (boundaries 50) is no longer consumed for geometry: the master at precedence 100 covers a superset of its footprint, so it would contribute nothing; its registration record stays for Stage B's independent text-mask cross-check. This record is MACHINE-FITTED by tools/fit_registration.py from tools/registration/seeds/wh3_dlc_ie_parchment_map_english.json; re-derive rather than hand-edit. FIT: {\"anisotropy_p99\": 3.0, \"coarse_iou\": 0.5148, \"folded_fraction\": 0.0, \"landmark_check_px\": {\"max\": 1210.0, \"mean\": 555.2}, \"landmarks\": 12, \"lattice\": \"10x8\", \"method\": \"coarse affine + thin-plate lattice refined on two-sided silhouette IoU\", \"move\": {\"max_px\": 623.0762393158641, \"mean_px\": 207.55517166096905, \"n\": 80, \"p90_px\": 367.7002353651541}, \"refined_iou\": 0.6732}",
